<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">title</ansi>

Your title reflects who you are — it is earned, not chosen.
It has three parts:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Mutation Tier</ansi>  Based on your total mutation load.
                  Awakened, Evolved, Ascendant, or Exalted.
                  No mutations means no prefix.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Skill Tier</ansi>    Based on aggregate skill progress across
                  all 17 skills. Ranges from scrub to master.

  <ansi fg="yellow">Archetype</ansi>     Based on which stats you lean toward.
                  Warriors favor Strength, rogues favor
                  Dexterity, channelers favor Willpower, etc.
                  Balanced builds may produce hybrid archetypes
                  like paladin, duelist, or sage.

<ansi fg="yellow">Example titles:</ansi>
  scrub warrior         — new character, Strength-focused
  Awakened expert sage  — mutated, skilled, Willpower+Charisma
  Exalted master duelist — heavily mutated, max skills, Str+Dex

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>
  <ansi fg="command">title</ansi>   — view your current title and breakdown

<ansi fg="yellow">Archetypes:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="white-bold">Pure:</ansi>   warrior, rogue, scout, guardian, channeler,
          orator
  <ansi fg="white-bold">Hybrid:</ansi> paladin, juggernaut, duelist, ranger, sage,
          seer, stoic
  <ansi fg="white-bold">Even:</ansi>   generalist

